From: Dmytro Kostyshyn <dimakostishen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:27:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Chunk store hook: chunks saved somewhere other than region
 files

A crate above the engine can offer a `horizon_hooks::storage::ChunkStore`
(`Hooks::chunk_store`); the save layer then reads and writes chunk records
(region, entities, poi) through it instead of the world's region files, as
uncompressed named NBT. The far view and the old-chunk scan ask it which
chunks of a region are saved. Without a registered store nothing changes.

For servers that share one world through a database (Sculk's AnvilDB).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
